>>
Rule 1 (padding should be non-negative integer or a tuple of four non-negative integers)
{v_1 : int ⊎ tuple(int)} |= (v_1 ≥ 0) ∨ (v_1.len = 4 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : v_1[i] ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 2 (tensor dimension should be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (Padding should be less than or equal to two times the input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2 ≤ 2 * shape(v_1, 0)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 2 * shape(v_1, 0) ∧ v_2 ≤ 2 * shape(v_1, 1))
>>
Rule 4 (Padding values should result in non-negative output dimensions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ tuple(int)} |= if v_2.len = 1 then shape(v_1, 2) + 2 * v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) + 2 * v_2 ≥ 0 else shape(v_1, 2) + v_2[2] + v_2[3] ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) + v_2[0] + v_2[1] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (Tuple padding length should be 4)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 4
>>
Rule 6 (Tuple padding values should result in non-negative output dimensions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= shape(v_1, 2) + v_2[0] + v_2[1] ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) + v_2[2] + v_2[3] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 7 (If input tensor is 1D, padding cannot be a tuple)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ 1
>>
Rule 8 (Input tensor dimensions should be either 2 or 3 when padding is used)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 3 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 9 (When tensor is 4D, each dimension of padding should be less than or equal to the corresponding input dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then v_2[0] ≤ shape(v_1, 3) ∧ v_2[1] ≤ shape(v_1, 3) ∧ v_2[2] ≤ shape(v_1, 2) ∧ v_2[3] ≤ shape(v_1, 2)
